01:20:30,000 --> 01:20:36,000
Bird is a 1988 American biographical musical drama film about jazz saxophonist Charlie "Bird"
Parker, directed and produced by Clint Eastwood and written by Joel Oliansky.

12
01:27:49,090 --> 01:27:55,090
The film stars Forest Whitaker as Parker, and
Diane Venora as his wife Chan Parker.

13
01:35:08,181 --> 01:35:14,181
It is constructed as a montage of scenes from Parker's life, from his
childhood in Kansas City, through his early death at the age of 34.

14
01:42:27,272 --> 01:42:33,272
The film moves back and forth through Parker's history,
blending moments to find some truth to his life.

15
01:49:46,363 --> 01:49:52,363
Much of the film revolves around his only grounding relationships with Chan, Bebop
pioneer trumpet player and band leader Dizzy Gillespie (Samuel E.

16
01:57:05,454 --> 01:57:11,454
Wright), and his influence (both musically and into the world of heroin
addiction) on trumpet player Red Rodney (Michael Zelniker).

17
02:04:24,545 --> 02:04:30,545
Despite a lukewarm commercial performance, the film was well received by critics, with
particular praise toward Whitaker's performance, which became his breakthrough role.

18
02:11:43,636 --> 02:11:49,636
He won the Best Actor Award at the 1988 Cannes Film Festival and was nominated for Best Actor – Motion
Picture Drama at the 46th Golden Globe Awards, while Eastwood won the award for Best Director.

19
02:19:02,727 --> 02:19:08,727
Cahiers du Cinéma ranked Bird at #5 on its end-of-year Top 10 List.

20
